#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186634557 :knowledge-point/canonical-example {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186634647 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186634557 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "fecaf27b-659c-59dd-887f-f154d5f83bd4" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Cross Product Equation of a Line That Passes Through Two Points"}] :question/id #uuid "96216bf8-a1cf-5704-8edb-81c3fbdebb58" :question/math-academy-id "e-4922" :question/problem "A line passes through the points $P(4,-7,9)$ and $Q(3,-5,8).$ Find its vector equation in the form $\\mathbf{r} \\times \\mathbf{v} = \\mathbf{c}.$" :question/worked-solution "We know that the line passes through the points $P(4,-7,9)$ and $Q(3,-5,8)$. Now, we need to find a vector parallel to the given line. We can use the vector $\\overrightarrow{PQ}$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}v & =\\overset{\\to }{PQ} \\\\  & =q-p \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}3 \\\\ -5 \\\\ 8\\end{bmatrix}-\\begin{bmatrix}4 \\\\ -7 \\\\ 9\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}-1 \\\\ 2 \\\\ -1\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, starting with the equation of the line using the cross product, we manipulate the equation and then substitute in our values of $\\mathbf{p}$ and $\\mathbf{v}$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(r-p)\\times v & =0 \\\\ r\\times v-p\\times v & =0 \\\\ r\\times v & =p\\times v \\\\ r\\times \\begin{bmatrix}-1 \\\\ 2 \\\\ -1\\end{bmatrix} & =\\begin{bmatrix}4 \\\\ -7 \\\\ 9\\end{bmatrix}\\times \\begin{bmatrix}-1 \\\\ 2 \\\\ -1\\end{bmatrix} \\\\ r\\times \\begin{bmatrix}-1 \\\\ 2 \\\\ -1\\end{bmatrix} & =\\begin{vmatrix}i & j & k \\\\ 4 & -7 & 9 \\\\ -1 & 2 & -1\\end{vmatrix} \\\\ r\\times \\begin{bmatrix}-1 \\\\ 2 \\\\ -1\\end{bmatrix} & =-11i-5j+k\\end{aligned}\n$$"} :knowledge-point/id #uuid "fecaf27b-659c-59dd-887f-f154d5f83bd4" :knowledge-point/questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186634581 :question/math-academy-id "q-104100"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186634593 :question/math-academy-id "q-104101"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186634637 :question/math-academy-id "q-72127"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186634679 :question/math-academy-id "q-32933"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186642312 :question/math-academy-id "q-32928"}] :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Cross Product Equation of a Line That Passes Through Two Points"}]}
